.TH MCHD 8 "2026-05-23" "meshherder 0.1.0" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
mchd \- Mesh Herder daemon for managing MeshCore repeater nodes
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mchd
[\fB--config\fR \fIPATH\fR]
[\fB--log-level\fR \fILEVEL\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mchd
is the Mesh Herder daemon. It opens one serial connection to the local MeshCore
gateway node, reads desired fleet state from
.IR config.yaml ,
stores observed state in SQLite, and processes managed nodes one at a time.
.PP
When enabled in configuration, mchd also serves a read-only HTTP JSON API on a
loopback address for local integrations and future user interfaces. It does
not expose sync, command execution, commissioning, or other mutating actions.
.PP
The daemon owns all gateway traffic. The
.BR mch (1)
command talks to
.B mchd
over a Unix socket for status, validation-independent operations, sync requests,
commissioning, and carefully checked one-off commands.
.PP
Configuration files remain operator-owned. The daemon reads
.I config.yaml
and
.I secrets.yaml
on startup and hot-reloads them after file changes. If a reload fails
validation, the previous in-memory config remains active.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-c, \-\-config \fIPATH\fR
Path to
.IR config.yaml .
The packaged systemd unit uses
.IR /etc/meshherder/config.yaml .
.TP
.B \-\-log-level \fILEVEL\fR
Set logging level. Valid values are
.BR DEBUG ,
.BR INFO ,
.BR WARNING ,
and
.BR ERROR .
The default is
.BR INFO .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/meshherder/config.yaml
Desired fleet state. This includes gateway settings, scheduler settings, groups,
nodes, facts to collect, messenger settings, and paths such as
.I db_path
and
.IR socket_path .
An optional
.I api
mapping enables the loopback-only read-only HTTP API and selects its host and
port.
.TP
.I /etc/meshherder/secrets.yaml
Node passwords and private keys. This file is usually mode 600 and owned by the
service account.
.TP
.I /var/lib/meshherder/mch.db
SQLite database containing observed node state, collected facts, command
history, settings state, logs, and sync schedule.
.TP
.I /run/meshherder/mchd.sock
Default Unix socket used by
.BR mch (1).
.TP
.I /dev/meshcore0
Recommended stable symlink for the USB-attached gateway node.
.SH READ-ONLY API
The HTTP API is disabled by default. Enable it in
.I config.yaml
with:
.PP
.nf
api:
  enabled: true
  host: 127.0.0.1
  port: 8743
.fi
.PP
Only loopback hosts are accepted until API authentication is implemented.
Available read-only endpoints are:
.PP
.nf
GET /healthz
GET /api/v1/fleet
GET /api/v1/nodes/<label-or-pubkey-prefix>
GET /api/v1/issues
GET /api/v1/plan
GET /api/v1/logs?node=<label-or-prefix>&limit=50
.fi
.PP
The fleet response includes
.B schema_version: 1
and normalized node health, facts, setting classifications, planned actions,
and issues suitable for presentation by a dashboard.
.SH SYSTEMD
The packaged service unit is named
.BR mchd.service .
Install and start it with:
.PP
.nf
sudo cp systemd/mchd.service /etc/systemd/system/
sudo systemctl daemon-reload
sudo systemctl enable --now mchd
.fi
.PP
Check status and follow logs with:
.PP
.nf
systemctl status mchd
journalctl -u mchd -f
.fi
.PP
The unit runs as the
.B mch
system user, grants serial access through the
.B dialout
group, creates
.IR /run/meshherder ,
and keeps
.I /etc/meshherder
read-only to the daemon.
.SH RELOAD
.B mchd
watches
.I config.yaml
and
.I secrets.yaml
and reloads them shortly after changes. You can also force a reload with:
.PP
.nf
sudo systemctl kill -s HUP mchd
.fi
.PP
Gateway device, database path, socket path, and API listener changes require a daemon restart.
.SH OPERATION
The daemon processes nodes sequentially to avoid hammering the mesh. Between
nodes it waits the configured
.I inter_node_delay_seconds
unless there is only one node in the run.
.PP
Manual sync, scheduled sync, raw exec, and commissioning share one high-level
gateway operation lock. If another workflow owns the gateway, CLI operations
return a
.B busy
message instead of overlapping radio traffic.
.SH TROUBLESHOOTING
.TP
.B Cannot connect to daemon
Check that
.B mchd.service
is running and that your user is in the
.B mch
group so it can access the Unix socket.
.TP
.B Gateway device missing
Check the USB device and the
.I /dev/meshcore0
udev symlink. The systemd unit waits for
.I dev-meshcore0.device
when the recommended udev rule is installed.
.TP
.B Config reload failed
Run
.B mch validate
or
.B sudo mch validate
to check config and secrets. The daemon keeps the last valid config after a bad
reload.
.TP
.B Daemon exits on startup after a config error
Startup config errors are permanent operator errors, so the systemd unit does
not restart-loop on them. Run
.B mch validate
to fix the config, then restart
.B mchd.service .
.TP
.B Node remains partial
Use
.B mch logs \fILABEL_OR_PREFIX\fR
to inspect recent per-node activity and failed commands.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mch (1),
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR journalctl (1)
